body:
## 2026-09-07 readability and accessible feedback
Use the existing P3Combat presentation actors, cues, health read models and HUD. Coordinate animation through #2610, not a second animation controller.

Evaluate at ordinary speed/distance with the selected roster and real meteor/ability set:
- distinguish caster/team, target/danger area, cast versus impact, hit versus miss, invulnerability/block/cooldown where applicable;
- first-person hands/body/effects and third-person camera collision must not obscure aim or essential enemy tells;
- communicate damage direction, health/result and resource/cooldown through readable shape/text/icon/timing as well as color; critical information must not rely on audio or color alone;
- retain useful sound/impact cues but avoid repeated cue spam or effects that hide Core/creep/contact state;
- expose existing sensitivity, camera/FOV and readability settings coherently where supported; do not turn this into a settings framework.

Capture one attacker/observer sequence in each view and record concrete unreadable moments before tuning. Profile expensive VFX only if #2611 identifies the cost. P3CombatMeteorPresentationActor.cpp, P3CombatHUDWidget.cpp and P3LaneWarHUDWidget.cpp each serialize independently with current claimants.

---

Parent: #803 / #941. Coordinate with #956 and #1091. Reuse current P3Combat, spell, GameplayCue/VFX, health and HUD presentation owners; no new presentation framework.

Acceptance:
- the important live abilities have readable cast/start, travel/active and impact/result feedback where applicable;
- enemy hero/creep damage and defeat are understandable at normal gameplay distance and speed;
- cooldown/resource feedback is visible enough to make combat decisions without reading logs;
- first-person and third-person both remain usable and do not hide essential tells;
- fix concrete missing/weak cues found in a normal Lane War play pass using existing assets where practical.
